Package: basemapper
Title: Headless Spatial Basemap Renderer
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Pukar", "Bhandari", email = "arpuuuk@gmail.com",
  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Renders MapLibre GL styled basemaps (vector and raster tiles)
    headlessly with a Rust core: a software port of MapLibre GL JS's
    renderer, tested pixel by pixel against MapLibre GL JS. A basemap is an
    extent, a zoom (the detail) and a dpi (the sharpness), any three of
    extent, zoom, image size and dpi giving the fourth; it renders to PNG,
    arrays and rasters in any coordinate reference system, or to true vector
    SVG, and several styles can be stacked. In 'ggplot2' (ggplot() + m) and
    'tmap' v4 (tm_basemap()) plots it is warped into the plot's coordinate
    reference system and rendered at the output device's resolution.
URL: https://ar-puuk.github.io/basemapper/r/, https://github.com/ar-puuk/basemapper
BugReports: https://github.com/ar-puuk/basemapper/issues
